/-!
# The Rees presentation of a weight degeneration of a subalgebra

Give the variable `X s` of `MvPolynomial σ R` the weight `w s ∈ ℕ`, and let
`c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R` be a family with `c i` of weight at most `d i`, whose weighted
homogeneous component `g i` of weight `d i` is its *initial form*. Give the variable `Y i` of
`MvPolynomial ι R` the weight `d i`. The degeneration of the subalgebra `R[c]` towards the
subalgebra `R[g]` of initial forms is carried by the `R[t]`-algebra generated by the
`c i * t ^ d i`, inside the Rees algebra of the weight filtration. It is the image of the
*Rees presentation map* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightReesAeval c d`, the substitution
`Y i ↦ c i * t ^ d i`, `t ↦ t`, from `(MvPolynomial ι R)[t]` to `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]`, whose
kernel this file computes.

Suppose the relations among the initial forms, the kernel of `aeval g`, are generated by
polynomials `r j` which are weighted homogeneous of weight `e j`, and that each `aeval c (r j)` is
the image `aeval c (Q j)` of a polynomial `Q j` all of whose exponents have weight below `e j`.
The lifted relations `r j - Q j` then have weight `e j`, with top component `r j`. Their
homogenizations `G j = ∑ q_x Y^x t^(e j - weight d x)` lie in the kernel of the Rees presentation
map, and this file proves that they generate the whole kernel
(`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span`). Since the kernel of a map into the
`t`-torsion-free ring `(MvPolynomial σ R)[t]` is `t`-saturated, so is the ideal generated by the
`G j`. Setting `t = 1` turns `G j` into `r j - Q j`, and setting `t = 0` turns it into `r j`
(`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.coeff_zero_weightHomogenization_sub`).

The main input is the **standard representation** with respect to the weight, proved by induction
on the weight `n`: a polynomial `P` of weight at most `n` with `aeval c P = 0` is a combination
`∑ j, h j * (r j - Q j)` in which every exponent `x` of `h j` satisfies `weight d x + e j ≤ n`.
The weighted homogeneous component of weight `n` of `aeval c P` is `aeval g` of the component of
weight `n` of `P`
(`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval_of_mem_weightFiltration`), so if it
vanishes, that component of `P` is a combination of the `r j`, which is cancelled by the
same combination of the `r j - Q j` up to terms of smaller weight.

For a monic family `c` with leading exponents `a i = m.degree (c i)` for a monomial order `m`, the
initial forms are the monomials `X^(a i)`, their relations form the toric ideal, generated by
binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)`, and the SAGBI criterion supplies certificates `Q j` whose exponents
`x` satisfy `A x ≺ A (u j)` for `A x = ∑ i, x i • a i`. Only finitely many strict comparisons
occur: the non-leading exponents of the `c i` and the exponents of the `Q j`. They are realized by a
weight vector with positive entries (`MonomialOrder.exists_pos_weight_lt`), which yields the
weight hypotheses above (`MonomialOrder.exists_pos_weight_forall_mem_weightFiltrationLT`). Then
`TauCeti.MvPolynomial.ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span_of_toricIdeal_eq_span` presents the algebra
generated by `t` and the `c i * t ^ d i` by relations which are the toric binomials at `t = 0` and
the lifted relations `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j) - Q j` of `R[c]` at `t = 1`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.exists_finsupp_sum_eq_of_aeval_eq_zero_of_mem_weightFiltration`: standard
  representations of the elements of the kernel of `aeval c` with respect to the weight.
* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span`: the homogenized lifted relations generate
  the kernel of the Rees presentation map, and
  `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.X_mul_mem_span_weightHomogenization_iff`: the ideal they generate is
  `t`-saturated.
* `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span_of_toricIdeal_eq_span`: the case of monomial
  initial forms and toric binomial relations.
* `MonomialOrder.exists_pos_weight_forall_mem_weightFiltrationLT`: for a finite monic family and
  finitely many bounded subduction certificates, a positive weight vector whose initial forms are
  the leading monomials and for which the certificates have smaller weight.

## References

* B. Sturmfels, *Gröbner Bases and Convex Polytopes*, University Lecture Series 8, AMS, 1996,
  Chapter 11 (the flat degeneration of a subalgebra to its initial algebra).
* L. Robbiano, M. Sweedler, *Subalgebra bases*, in *Commutative Algebra (Salvador, 1988)*,
  Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1430, Springer, 1990, 61–87.
* W. Bruns, A. Conca, M. Lembo, arXiv:2504.10019, §2, for monic SAGBI families and bounded
  subduction.
-/

public section

open scoped Polynomial

namespace TauCeti.MvPolynomial

open _root_.MvPolynomial

variable {σ ι J R : Type*} [CommRing R] {w : σ → ℕ} {c g : ι → MvPolynomial σ R} {d : ι → ℕ}
  {r Q : J → MvPolynomial ι R} {e : J → ℕ}

/-- **The reduction step.** Let each `c i` have weight at most `d i` with component `g i` of
weight `d i`, let polynomials `r j`, weighted homogeneous of weight `e j`, generate the kernel of
`aeval g`, and let each `Q j` have weight less than `e j`. If `P` has weight at most `n` and the
component of weight `n` of `aeval c P` vanishes, then `P` is the sum of a combination
`∑ j, h j * (r j - Q j)`, every exponent `x` of `h j` satisfying `weight d x + e j = n`, and of a
polynomial of weight less than `n`. -/
theorem exists_finsupp_sub_sum_mem_weightFiltrationLT
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (hg : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d i) (c i) = g i)
    (hJ : RingHom.ker (aeval g) = Ideal.span (Set.range r))
    (hr : ∀ j, (r j).IsWeightedHomogeneous d (e j)) (hQ : ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R d (e j))
    {n : ℕ} {P : MvPolynomial ι R} (hP : P ∈ weightFiltration R d n)
    (hn : weightedHomogeneousComponent w n (aeval c P) = 0) :
    ∃ h : J →₀ MvPolynomial ι R, (∀ j, ∀ x ∈ (h j).support, Finsupp.weight d x + e j = n) ∧
      P - (h.sum fun j q ↦ q * (r j - Q j)) ∈ weightFiltrationLT R d n := by
  classical
  -- The part `P₀` of `P` of weight `n` is a relation among the `g i`: `P₀ = ∑ j, h j * r j`.
  have hP₀ : weightedHomogeneousComponent d n P ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range r) := by
    rw [← hJ, RingHom.mem_ker,
      ← weightedHomogeneousComponent_aeval_of_mem_weightFiltration hc hg hP, hn]
  obtain ⟨h, hsum, hdeg⟩ := exists_finsupp_sum_mul_eq_weightedHomogeneousComponent hr hP₀ n
  rw [weightedHomogeneousComponent_eq_self
    (weightedHomogeneousComponent_isWeightedHomogeneous _ _)] at hsum
  refine ⟨h, hdeg, ?_⟩
  -- `P - ∑ j, h j * (r j - Q j) = (P - P₀) + ∑ j, h j * Q j`.
  have heq : P - (h.sum fun j q ↦ q * (r j - Q j)) =
      (P - weightedHomogeneousComponent d n P) + h.sum fun j q ↦ q * Q j := by
    simp_rw [mul_sub]
    rw [Finsupp.sum_sub, hsum]
    ring
  rw [heq]
  refine add_mem (mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.2 fun x hx ↦ ?_)
    (Submodule.sum_mem _ fun j _ ↦ mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.2 fun x hx ↦ ?_)
  · rw [mem_support_iff, coeff_sub, coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent] at hx
    have hxn : Finsupp.weight d x ≠ n := fun h ↦ hx (by simp [h])
    have hxP : x ∈ P.support := mem_support_iff.2 fun h ↦ hx (by simp [h])
    exact lt_of_le_of_ne (mem_weightFiltration_iff.1 hP x hxP) hxn
  -- An exponent of `h j * Q j` is a sum `y + z` with `weight d y + e j = n` and
  -- `weight d z < e j`.
  · obtain ⟨y, hy, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_add.1 (support_mul _ _ hx)
    have := hdeg j y hy
    have := mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.1 (hQ j) z hz
    rw [map_add]
    omega

/-- **Standard representations.** Let each `c i` have weight at most `d i` with component `g i`
of weight `d i`, let polynomials `r j`, weighted homogeneous of weight `e j`, generate the kernel
of `aeval g`, and let `Q j` be polynomials of weight less than `e j` with
`aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (r j)`. If `P` has weight at most `n` and `aeval c P = 0`, then
`P = ∑ j, h j * (r j - Q j)` for some `h` such that every exponent `x` of `h j` satisfies
`weight d x + e j ≤ n`. -/
theorem exists_finsupp_sum_eq_of_aeval_eq_zero_of_mem_weightFiltration
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (hg : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d i) (c i) = g i)
    (hJ : RingHom.ker (aeval g) = Ideal.span (Set.range r))
    (hr : ∀ j, (r j).IsWeightedHomogeneous d (e j)) (hQ : ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R d (e j))
    (hQc : ∀ j, aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (r j)) {n : ℕ} {P : MvPolynomial ι R}
    (hP : P ∈ weightFiltration R d n) (hP0 : aeval c P = 0) :
    ∃ h : J →₀ MvPolynomial ι R, (h.sum fun j q ↦ q * (r j - Q j)) = P ∧
      ∀ j, ∀ x ∈ (h j).support, Finsupp.weight d x + e j ≤ n := by
  classical
  induction n generalizing P with
  | zero =>
    obtain ⟨h, hdeg, hlt⟩ := exists_finsupp_sub_sum_mem_weightFiltrationLT hc hg hJ hr hQ hP
      (by simp [hP0])
    rw [weightFiltrationLT_zero, Submodule.mem_bot, sub_eq_zero] at hlt
    exact ⟨h, hlt.symm, fun j x hx ↦ (hdeg j x hx).le⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    -- Remove the part of weight `n + 1`, then represent the rest, of weight at most `n`.
    obtain ⟨h₁, hdeg₁, hlt⟩ := exists_finsupp_sub_sum_mem_weightFiltrationLT hc hg hJ hr hQ hP
      (by simp [hP0])
    rw [weightFiltrationLT_succ] at hlt
    obtain ⟨h₂, hsum₂, hdeg₂⟩ := ih hlt (by simp [Finsupp.sum, hP0, hQc])
    refine ⟨h₁ + h₂, ?_, fun j x hx ↦ ?_⟩
    · rw [Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ ↦ zero_mul _) fun _ _ _ ↦ add_mul _ _ _, hsum₂,
        add_sub_cancel]
    · rw [Finsupp.add_apply] at hx
      rcases Finset.mem_union.1 (support_add hx) with hx | hx
      · exact (hdeg₁ j x hx).le
      · exact (hdeg₂ j x hx).trans n.le_succ

/-- **The Rees presentation.** Let each `c i` have weight at most `d i` with component `g i` of
weight `d i`, let polynomials `r j`, weighted homogeneous of weight `e j`, generate the kernel of
`aeval g`, and let `Q j` be polynomials of weight less than `e j` with
`aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (r j)`. Then the kernel of the Rees presentation map
`Y i ↦ c i * t ^ d i`, `t ↦ t` is generated by the homogenizations in degree `e j` of the lifted
relations `r j - Q j`. -/
theorem ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (hg : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d i) (c i) = g i)
    (hJ : RingHom.ker (aeval g) = Ideal.span (Set.range r))
    (hr : ∀ j, (r j).IsWeightedHomogeneous d (e j)) (hQ : ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R d (e j))
    (hQc : ∀ j, aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (r j)) :
    RingHom.ker (weightReesAeval c d) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ weightHomogenization R d (e j) (r j - Q j)) := by
  classical
  have hF (j : J) : r j - Q j ∈ weightFiltration R d (e j) := by
    rw [← weightFiltrationLT_sup_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule]
    exact sub_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_right ((mem_weightedHomogeneousSubmodule R d _ _).2 (hr j)))
      (Submodule.mem_sup_left (hQ j))
  refine le_antisymm (fun f hf ↦ ?_) (Ideal.span_le.2 ?_)
  · -- Decompose `f` by the weight `weight d x + k` of its monomials `Y^x tᵏ`: its part of weight
    -- `n` is the homogenization in degree `n` of the coefficient of `tⁿ` in `weightReesHom R d f`.
    set G := weightReesHom R d f
    have hG (n : ℕ) : G.coeff n ∈ weightFiltration R d n := by
      have : G ∈ weightReesAlgebra R d := by
        rw [← range_weightReesHom]
        exact AlgHom.mem_range_self _ f
      exact TauCeti.mem_coeffSubalgebra_iff.1 this n
    have hf' : f = ∑ n ∈ G.support, weightHomogenization R d n (G.coeff n) := by
      refine weightReesHom_injective R d ?_
      rw [map_sum]
      simp_rw [weightReesHom_weightHomogenization (hG _)]
      exact G.as_sum_support
    rw [hf']
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun n _ ↦ ?_
    -- The coefficient of `tⁿ` lies in the kernel of `aeval c`, so it has a standard
    -- representation, which homogenizes to a combination of the `G j`.
    have hG0 : aeval c (G.coeff n) = 0 := by
      have h0 : Polynomial.mapAlgHom (aeval c) G = 0 := by
        rw [← AlgHom.comp_apply, ← weightReesAeval_eq_comp]
        exact hf
      simpa using congr(Polynomial.coeff $h0 n)
    obtain ⟨h, hsum, hdeg⟩ :=
      exists_finsupp_sum_eq_of_aeval_eq_zero_of_mem_weightFiltration hc hg hJ hr hQ hQc (hG n) hG0
    rw [← hsum, Finsupp.sum, map_sum]
    refine Ideal.sum_mem _ fun j hj ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := support_nonempty.2 (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hj)
    have hle : e j ≤ n := le_trans (Nat.le_add_left _ _) (hdeg j x hx)
    have hhj : h j ∈ weightFiltration R d (n - e j) :=
      mem_weightFiltration_iff.2 fun y hy ↦ Nat.le_sub_of_add_le (hdeg j y hy)
    rw [← Nat.sub_add_cancel hle, weightHomogenization_mul hhj (hF j)]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩)
  · rintro _ ⟨j, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, weightReesAeval_weightHomogenization (hF j), map_sub,
      hQc, sub_self, Polynomial.monomial_zero_right]

/-- **`t`-saturation of the Rees presentation.** Under the hypotheses of
`ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span`, the ideal generated by the homogenized lifted relations is
saturated with respect to the Rees parameter `t`: `t * f` lies in it only if `f` does. -/
theorem X_mul_mem_span_weightHomogenization_iff
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (d i))
    (hg : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (d i) (c i) = g i)
    (hJ : RingHom.ker (aeval g) = Ideal.span (Set.range r))
    (hr : ∀ j, (r j).IsWeightedHomogeneous d (e j)) (hQ : ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R d (e j))
    (hQc : ∀ j, aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (r j)) {f : (MvPolynomial ι R)[X]} :
    Polynomial.X * f ∈
        Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ weightHomogenization R d (e j) (r j - Q j)) ↔
      f ∈ Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ weightHomogenization R d (e j) (r j - Q j)) := by
  rw [← ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span hc hg hJ hr hQ hQc, RingHom.mem_ker, RingHom.mem_ker,
    map_mul, weightReesAeval_X]
  exact ⟨fun h ↦ Polynomial.isRegular_X.left (h.trans (mul_zero _).symm),
    fun h ↦ by rw [h, mul_zero]⟩

variable {a : ι → σ →₀ ℕ} {u v : J → ι →₀ ℕ}

/-- **The Rees presentation for monomial initial forms.** Let each `c i` have weight at most
`weight w (a i)` with component `X^(a i)` of that weight, let binomials `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)`
generate the toric ideal of the exponents `a i`, and let `Q j` be polynomials of weight less than
that of `Y^(u j)`, for the weights `d i = weight w (a i)`, with
`aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (Y^(u j) - Y^(v j))`. Then the kernel of the Rees presentation map
`Y i ↦ c i * t ^ d i`, `t ↦ t` is generated by the homogenizations
`Y^(u j) - Y^(v j) - ∑ q_x Y^x t^(weight d (u j) - weight d x)` of the lifted relations. -/
theorem ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span_of_toricIdeal_eq_span
    (hc : ∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (Finsupp.weight w (a i)))
    (ha : ∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (Finsupp.weight w (a i)) (c i) = monomial (a i) 1)
    (hJ : TauCeti.toricIdeal R a =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1))
    (hQ : ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i))
      (Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i)) (u j)))
    (hQc : ∀ j, aeval c (Q j) = aeval c (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1)) :
    RingHom.ker (weightReesAeval c fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i)) =
      Ideal.span (Set.range fun j ↦ weightHomogenization R (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i))
        (Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i)) (u j))
        (monomial (u j) 1 - monomial (v j) 1 - Q j)) := by
  refine ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span hc ha
    (by rw [← TauCeti.toricIdeal_eq_ker_aeval_monomial, hJ]) (fun j ↦ ?_) hQ hQc
  -- The binomial `Y^(u j) - Y^(v j)` is weighted homogeneous, as `A (u j) = A (v j)`.
  rcases subsingleton_or_nontrivial R with hR | hR
  · rw [Subsingleton.elim (monomial (u j) (1 : R) - monomial (v j) 1) 0]
    exact isWeightedHomogeneous_zero R _ _
  have huv : Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a (u j) = Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a (v j) :=
    TauCeti.monomial_sub_monomial_mem_toricIdeal_iff.1
      (by rw [hJ]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩)
  have hw (x : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i)) x =
      Finsupp.weight w (Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a x) :=
    Finsupp.weight_comp_eq_apply_linearCombination (Finsupp.weight w) a x
  exact (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ rfl).sub
    (isWeightedHomogeneous_monomial _ _ _ (by rw [hw, hw, huv]))

end TauCeti.MvPolynomial

namespace MonomialOrder

open _root_.MvPolynomial TauCeti.MvPolynomial

variable {σ ι J R : Type*} {m : MonomialOrder σ} [CommSemiring R] {c : ι → MvPolynomial σ R}

/-- **Weights for a SAGBI degeneration.** Let `c` be a finite monic family with leading exponents
`a i = m.degree (c i)`, write `A x = ∑ i, x i • a i`, and let `Q j`, finitely many, be polynomials
all of whose exponents `x` satisfy `A x ≺ A (u j)`. Then some weight vector `w` with positive
entries makes `X^(a i)` the component of `c i` of its top weight `weight w (a i)`, and makes every
`Q j` of weight less than that of `Y^(u j)` for the weights `d i = weight w (a i)`. These are the
weight hypotheses of `TauCeti.MvPolynomial.ker_weightReesAeval_eq_span_of_toricIdeal_eq_span`. -/
theorem exists_pos_weight_forall_mem_weightFiltrationLT [Finite ι] [Finite J]
    (hc : ∀ i, m.Monic (c i)) {u : J → ι →₀ ℕ} {Q : J → MvPolynomial ι R}
    (hQ : ∀ j, ∀ x ∈ (Q j).support, Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) x ≺[m]
      Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ (fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)) (u j)) :
    ∃ w : σ → ℕ, (∀ s, 0 < w s) ∧
      (∀ i, c i ∈ weightFiltration R w (Finsupp.weight w (m.degree (c i)))) ∧
      (∀ i, weightedHomogeneousComponent w (Finsupp.weight w (m.degree (c i))) (c i) =
        monomial (m.degree (c i)) 1) ∧
      ∀ j, Q j ∈ weightFiltrationLT R (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (m.degree (c i)))
        (Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (m.degree (c i))) (u j)) := by
  classical
  set a := fun i ↦ m.degree (c i)
  set A := Finsupp.linearCombination ℕ a
  cases nonempty_fintype ι
  cases nonempty_fintype J
  -- The finitely many comparisons: the non-leading exponents of the `c i`, and the exponents of
  -- the `Q j`.
  let K := (Σ i, (c i).support.erase (a i)) ⊕ (Σ j, (Q j).support)
  let lhs : K → σ →₀ ℕ := Sum.elim (fun k ↦ k.2) fun k ↦ A k.2
  let rhs : K → σ →₀ ℕ := Sum.elim (fun k ↦ a k.1) fun k ↦ A (u k.1)
  have hlt (k : K) : lhs k ≺[m] rhs k := by
    rcases k with ⟨i, γ, hγ⟩ | ⟨j, x, hx⟩
    · obtain ⟨hne, hγ⟩ := Finset.mem_erase.1 hγ
      exact lt_of_le_of_ne (m.le_degree hγ) (fun h ↦ hne (m.toSyn.injective h))
    · exact hQ j x hx
  obtain ⟨w, hw, hwlt⟩ := m.exists_pos_weight_lt hlt
  have hcw (i : ι) (γ : σ →₀ ℕ) (hγ : γ ∈ (c i).support) (hne : γ ≠ a i) :
      Finsupp.weight w γ < Finsupp.weight w (a i) :=
    hwlt (Sum.inl ⟨i, γ, Finset.mem_erase.2 ⟨hne, hγ⟩⟩)
  refine ⟨w, hw, fun i ↦ mem_weightFiltration_iff.2 fun γ hγ ↦ ?_, fun i ↦ ?_,
    fun j ↦ mem_weightFiltrationLT_iff.2 fun x hx ↦ ?_⟩
  · rcases eq_or_ne γ (a i) with rfl | hne
    · exact le_rfl
    · exact (hcw i γ hγ hne).le
  · ext γ
    rw [coeff_weightedHomogeneousComponent, coeff_monomial]
    rcases eq_or_ne γ (a i) with rfl | hne
    · simp [a, (hc i).coeff_degree]
    · simp only [show m.degree (c i) ≠ γ from hne.symm, ↓reduceIte, ite_eq_right_iff]
      intro hγw
      by_contra hγ
      exact (hcw i γ (mem_support_iff.2 hγ) hne).ne hγw
  · have hW (y : ι →₀ ℕ) : Finsupp.weight (fun i ↦ Finsupp.weight w (a i)) y =
        Finsupp.weight w (A y) :=
      Finsupp.weight_comp_eq_apply_linearCombination (Finsupp.weight w) a y
    rw [hW, hW]
    exact hwlt (Sum.inr ⟨j, x, hx⟩)

end MonomialOrder
